WEBVTT

00:00:00.597 --> 00:00:04.287
Some simple PostgreSQL views are automatically updatable.

00:00:04.287 --> 00:00:07.652
A write through the view can flow to the underlying table.

00:00:07.652 --> 00:00:12.237
But this is not true for every view.

00:00:12.237 --> 00:00:16.147
Joins, aggregates, grouping, and other features can make a view non-updatable.

00:00:16.147 --> 00:00:20.782
Treat writable views as a deliberate interface and test their behavior.

00:00:20.782 --> 00:00:25.872
A standard view stores a query definition, not a separate copy of the rows.

00:00:25.872 --> 00:00:32.342
Treat the selected columns, names, types, and grain as a contract with downstream users.

00:00:32.342 --> 00:00:38.556
Changing that contract can break dashboards or applications even if the underlying query still runs.
